)','The push() method is used to add data to a Stack.'),(644,16,'What is the difference between pop() and peek() in Stack?','MEDIUM','pop() removes the last element, while peek() only fetches it','The notes state that pop() removes the last data, whereas peek() fetches it without removing it.'),(645,16,'Set is a sub-interface of which interface?','EASY','Collection interface','Set is a sub-interface of Collection.'),(646,16,'Which data structure does the Set interface follow according to the notes?','EASY','Non-linear data structure','The notes describe Set as following a non-linear data structure.'),(647,16,'Which statement describes the characteristics of Set?','MEDIUM','Insertion order is not maintained, duplicates are not allowed and it is not index based','Set does not maintain insertion order, does not allow duplicates and is not index based.'),(648,16,'How many null values can be added to a Set according to the notes?','EASY','Only one null value','The notes state that only one null can be added to a Set.'),(649,16,'Which are the implementation classes of Set?','EASY','HashSet, LinkedHashSet and TreeSet','The notes list HashSet, LinkedHashSet and TreeSet as Set implementation classes.'),(650,16,'Which Set implementation maintains insertion order?','EASY','LinkedHashSet','LinkedHashSet uses a hashtable and doubly linked structure to maintain insertion order.'),(651,16,'Which Set implementation stores elements in natural ascending order?','EASY','TreeSet','TreeSet follows natural sorting order, which is ascending order.'),(652,16,'What is the initial capacity of HashSet?','MEDIUM','16','The notes specify an initial capacity of 16 for HashSet.'),(653,16,'What is the load factor of HashSet mentioned in the notes?','MEDIUM','0.75 or 75%','The load factor or fill ratio of HashSet is 0.75 (75%).'),(654,16,'What happens when a null value is added to TreeSet according to the notes?','HARD','NullPointerException occurs','The notes state that TreeSet does not accept nul