HECK is assigned to a column along with a condition.'),(1068,37,'What happens when a value satisfies the CHECK constraint condition?','MEDIUM','C','The CHECK constraint accepts a value when its condition is satisfied.'),(1069,37,'What is the main purpose of a Primary Key?','EASY','A','A Primary Key is used to identify records uniquely from a table.'),(1070,37,'A Primary Key is a combination of which two constraints?','MEDIUM','D','The notes describe Primary Key as a combination of UNIQUE and NOT NULL.'),(1071,37,'What is the purpose of a Foreign Key?','EASY','B','A Foreign Key is used to establish a connection between tables.'),(1072,37,'Where is a Foreign Key present according to the notes?','MEDIUM','C','A Foreign Key is present in the child table but belongs to the parent table.'),(1073,37,'How many subsets or languages of SQL are listed in the notes?','EASY','C','The five subsets are DDL, DML, DCL, TCL and DQL.'),(1074,37,'What is the full form of DDL?','EASY','A','DDL stands for Data Definition Language.'),(1075,37,'What is the main purpose of DDL?','MEDIUM','B','DDL is used to create or alter the structure of a table.'),(1076,37,'Which of the following commands belongs to DDL?','EASY','D','CREATE, ALTER, RENAME, TRUNCATE and DROP are listed as DDL commands.'),(1077,37,'What is the full form of DML?','EASY','C','DML stands for Data Manipulation Language.'),(1078,37,'Which set contains only DML commands according to the notes?','MEDIUM','A','INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE are the three DML commands listed in the notes.'),(1079,37,'What is the purpose of DCL?','MEDIUM','B','DCL is used to control access over the data.'),(1080,37,'Which commands are included in DCL?','EASY','D','GRANT and REVOKE are the two DCL commands listed in the notes.'),(1081,37,'Which of the following is a TCL command?','EASY','A','COMMIT, ROLLBACK and SAVEPOINT are the TCL commands listed in the notes.'),(1082,37,'What is the purpose of DQL?','MEDIUM','C','DQL is used to fetch or retrieve data 