he FROM clause.'),(1096,37,'How does the WHERE clause execute according to the notes?','EASY','D','The WHERE clause executes row by row.'),(1097,37,'Which operators can be used to combine multiple conditions in a WHERE clause?','EASY','B','Logical operators are used to combine multiple conditions in WHERE.'),(1098,37,'Which is a valid filter-condition format shown in the notes?','MEDIUM','A','A filter condition can compare a column or expression with a value.'),(1099,37,'Which of the following is another valid filter-condition format?','MEDIUM','C','The notes also allow comparison between two column names or expressions.'),(1100,37,'Which logical operator returns TRUE only when all conditions are satisfied?','EASY','D','AND returns TRUE when all the conditions are satisfied.'),(1101,37,'What is the minimum number of conditions required to use AND?','EASY','B','According to the notes, AND requires a minimum of two conditions.'),(1102,37,'What happens when AND and OR are used together without appropriate brackets, according to the notes?','MEDIUM','A','The notes state that AND gets the first execution priority, which may produce invalid output. Brackets are suggested for OR conditions.'),(1103,37,'How many types of SQL operators are listed in the notes?','EASY','C','The notes list eight types of SQL operators.'),(1104,37,'Which of the following is an arithmetic operator in SQL?','EASY','A','The arithmetic operators listed are +, -, * and /.'),(1105,37,'Which operators are listed as comparison operators in the notes?','EASY','B','The comparison operators listed are = and !=.'),(1106,37,'Which of the following is a relational operator?','EASY','D','The relational operators listed are >, <, >= and <=.'),(1107,37,'Which symbol is used as the concatenation operator in the notes?','EASY','C','The concatenation operator listed in the notes is ||.'),(1108,37,'Which of the following contains only logical operators?','EASY','A','AND, OR and NOT are the logical operators listed 