r listed in the notes?','EASY','C','LIKE is included in the list of special operators.'),(1123,37,'What is the DUAL table?','EASY','B','DUAL is a dummy table containing only one column. It is used when the value is not present in any table.'),(1124,37,'Which function retrieves the number of characters or digits from a given string?','EASY','A','LENGTH() returns the number of characters or digits in a given string.'),(1125,37,'What is the output of SELECT LENGTH(\'QST\') FROM DUAL according to the notes?','EASY','C','The string QST contains three characters.'),(1126,37,'What is the purpose of the CONCAT() function?','EASY','D','CONCAT() is used to join two strings only.'),(1127,37,'Which operator is suggested in the notes for concatenating more than two strings?','MEDIUM','B','The notes suggest using the concatenation operator (||) for more than two strings.'),(1128,37,'Which function converts a given string into uppercase?','EASY','A','UPPER() converts the given string to uppercase.'),(1129,37,'Which function converts a given string into lowercase?','EASY','C','LOWER() converts the given string to lowercase.'),(1130,37,'What does INITCAP() do?','MEDIUM','D','INITCAP() converts the first letter of a given string into an initial capital letter and the remaining characters into small letters.'),(1131,37,'Which function reverses a given string?','EASY','B','REVERSE() is used to reverse or transpose the given string.'),(1132,37,'What is the purpose of the MOD() function?','EASY','A','MOD() retrieves the modulus or remainder of two numeric values.'),(1133,37,'Which function retrieves the remainder of two numbers?','EASY','B','MOD() retrieves the modulus or remainder of two numeric values.'),(1134,37,'What is the output of SELECT MOD(4,2) FROM DUAL?','EASY','C','MOD(4,2) returns the remainder, which is 0.'),(1135,37,'Which condition retrieves employees having even employee numbers according to the notes?','MEDIUM','A','The notes use MOD(EMPNO,2) = 0 to retrieve even employee numbers.'),(1136,37,'Which function rounds a number based on its decimal value?','EASY','D','ROUND() rounds a number based on the decimal value.'),(1137,37,'What is the output of SELECT ROUND(8.4) FROM DUAL according to the notes?','EASY','B','A decimal value less than 0.5 rounds down to the same integer value.'),(1138,37,'What is the output of SELECT ROUND(8.5) FROM DUAL according to the notes?','EASY','C','A decimal value greater than or equal to 0.5 rounds up to the next number.'),(1139,37,'Which function cuts off the decimal part without rounding up?','EASY','A','TRUNC() cuts off the decimal part irrespective of its value.'),(1140,37,'What is the output of SELECT TRUNC(8.8) FROM DUAL according to the notes?','EASY','D','TRUNC(8.8) returns 8 by cutting off the decimal part.'),(1141,37,'Which statement correctly describes ROUND() and TRUNC()?','MEDIUM','B','ROUND() depends on the decimal value, whereas TRUNC() always cuts off the decimal part.'),(1142,37,'What is the output of SELECT TRUNC(6.9) FROM DUAL according to the notes?','EASY','A','The notes give TRUNC(6.9) as 6.'),(1143,37,'Which function is used to add a number of months to a given date?','EASY','B','ADD_MONTHS() adds a specified number of months to a given date.'),(1144,37,'What does MONTHS_BETWEEN() return?','EASY','C','MONTHS_BETWEEN() retrieves the number of months between two date values.'),(1145,37,'Which function retrieves the last date of a given month?','EASY','A','LAST_DAY() returns the last date of the month for the given date.'),(1146,37,'According to the notes, what is the result of LAST_DAY(\'14-FEB-24\')?','MEDIUM','D','The notes show that the last date of February 2024 is 29-FEB-24.'),(1147,37,'Which function converts a given date into a string using a format model?','EASY','B','TO_CHAR() converts a date into a string in the specified format model.'),(1148,37,'Which TO_CHAR() format model represents a four-digit year?','EASY','C','YYYY represents the year using four digits.'),(1149,37