 does HTML stand for?','EASY','B','HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.'),(1838,12,'What is the main purpose of HTML?','EASY','C','HTML is used to create the structure of a webpage.'),(1839,12,'Why is HTML not considered a programming language according to the notes?','EASY','A','HTML does not involve writing logic; it creates webpage structure using tags.'),(1840,12,'What is hypertext?','EASY','D','Any text that contains a link to another webpage is called hypertext.'),(1841,12,'Which tag is the root tag of an HTML document?','EASY','B','The html tag is the root tag and contains the document content.'),(1842,12,'Which section provides information about the HTML document?','EASY','A','The head tag provides information about the HTML document.'),(1843,12,'Which tag defines the document name displayed in the browser tab?','EASY','C','The title tag provides the document name shown in the browser tab.'),(1844,12,'Why is the meta tag described as an unpaired tag in the notes?','MEDIUM','D','The notes describe meta as having only an opening tag.'),(1845,12,'Which tag contains the content displayed on the webpage UI?','EASY','B','The body tag contains the HTML content displayed on the webpage.'),(1846,12,'What does <!DOCTYPE html> indicate according to the notes?','EASY','A','It tells the version of HTML; the notes identify HTML5 as the current version.'),(1847,12,'What are HTML tags?','EASY','C','Tags are predefined words enclosed within angular brackets.'),(1848,12,'What are the two types of HTML tags mentioned in the notes?','EASY','D','The two types are paired tags and unpaired or self-closing tags.'),(1849,12,'Which of the following is an example of an unpaired tag from the notes?','EASY','A','br, hr and meta are listed as unpaired tags.'),(1850,12,'What is an HTML element?','EASY','B','An element is a combination of tags and content.'),(1851,12,'Which three types of elements are listed in the notes?','EASY','C','The notes list inline, block and inline-block level elements.'),(1852,12,'Which statement describes inline-level elements?','MEDIUM','A','Inline elements display on the same line, and height and width cannot be provided according to the notes.'),(1853,12,'Which statement describes block-level elements?','MEDIUM','D','Block elements display on the next line, can have height and width, and occupy the full parent width.'),(1854,12,'Which elements are given as examples of inline-block elements in the notes?','EASY','B','Button and input are listed as inline-block examples.'),(1855,12,'Where are HTML attributes written?','EASY','C','Attributes provide extra information and are written in the opening tag.'),(1856,12,'How many heading tags are available in HTML according to the notes?','EASY','A','There are six heading tags, from h1 to h6.'),(1857,12,'What are formatting tags used for in HTML?','EASY','B','Formatting tags are used to change the appearance or format of text.'),(1858,12,'Which HTML tag makes text bold?','EASY','A','The b tag makes text bold.'),(1859,12,'Which tag also makes text bold according to the notes?','EASY','C','The strong tag also makes text bold.'),(1860,12,'Which pair of tags is used to underline text?','EASY','D','The u and ins tags provide underline formatting.'),(1861,12,'Which pair of tags makes text italic?','EASY','B','The i and em tags are used to make text italic.'),(1862,12,'Which tag highlights text?','EASY','A','The mark tag provides a highlight to text.'),(1863,12,'Which HTML tag provides double quotes around text?','EASY','C','The q tag provides double quotes around the text.'),(1864,12,'Which tag is used to write text as a power or superscript?','EASY','D','The sup tag writes text to the power of another text.'),(1865,12,'Which tag writes text at the base of another text?','EASY','B','The sub tag writes text at the base of another text.'),(1866,12,'Which tag provides a strike through text?','EASY','A','The del tag provides a strike through text. The notes also mention strike as deprecated.'),(1867,12,'Which tag displays content exactly as written and uses a monospace font according to the notes?','MEDIUM','C','The pre tag displays pre-formatted content using a monospace font.'),(1868,12,'How many heading tags are available in HTML?','EASY','B','HTML provides six heading tags, from h1 to h6.'),(1869,12,'Which heading tag is the largest according to the notes?','EASY','A','h1 is the largest heading tag, while h6 is the smallest.'),(1870,12,'What is the default size of the paragraph tag according to the notes?','MEDIUM','D','The notes specify the paragraph tag size as 16px.'),(1871,12,'Which HTML tag is used to add an image?','EASY','C','The img tag is used to add an image to a webpage.'),(1872,12,'What is the purpose of the src attribute in the img tag?','EASY','A','src specifies the path of the image.'),(1873,12,'What is the purpose of the alt attribute in an img tag?','MEDIUM','B','alt provides an alternate message displayed if the image does not load.'),(1874,12,'Which attributes are used to resize an image according to the notes?','EASY','C','The height and width attributes are used to resize an image.'),(1875,12,'What is the purpose of the marquee tag?','EASY','D','The marquee tag is used for scrolling content on a webpage.'),(1876,12,'What is the default scrolling direction of marquee content?','EASY','A','According to the notes, marquee content scrolls from right to left by default.'),(1877,12,'How many types of HTML lists are mentioned in the notes?','EASY','C','There are three types: ordered, unordered and description lists.'),(1878,12,'Which tag is used to create an ordered list?','EASY','A','The ol tag creates an ordered list, with li defining its items.'),(1879,12,'Which tag is used to define items inside an ordered list?','EASY','B','The li tag creates individual list items inside an ordered list.'),(1880,12,'What is the default type of an ordered list?','EASY','D','The default ordered list style is numbers.'),(1881,12,'Which attribute specifies the starting value of an ordered list?','EASY','C','The start attribute specifies the starting value of the list style.'),(1882,12,'Which attribute displays an ordered list in reverse order?','EASY','A','The reversed attribute displays the list style in reverse order.'),(1883,12,'Which tag creates an unordered list?','EASY','B','The ul tag creates an unordered list, which displays bullet points by default.'),(1884,12,'What is the default type of an unordered list according to the notes?','EASY','C','The default unordered list type is disc.'),(1885,12,'Which tag defines the description term in a description list?','EASY','A','The dt tag defines the description term.'),(1886,12,'Which tag provides information or a definition for a term in a description list?','EASY','D','The dd tag provides the description definition or information about the term.'),(1887,12,'Which HTML tag is used to create a hyperlink?','EASY','B','The anchor tag a is used to create hyperlinks.'),(1888,12,'Which attribute specifies the destination path in an anchor tag?','EASY','C','The href attribute specifies the path of the page where navigation should happen.'),(1889,12,'What is the default value of the target attribute in an anchor tag?','MEDIUM','A','The default target value is _self, which opens the page in the same tab.'),(1890,12,'Which target attribute value opens a linked page in a new tab?','EASY','D','_blank opens the linked page in a new tab according to the notes.'),(1891,12,'What is the purpose of the title attribute in an anchor tag?','MEDIUM','B','The title attribute displays a message when the mouse cursor is placed over the hyperlink.'),(1892,12,'What is the purpose of the br tag?','EASY','C','The br tag breaks the line so that the following content appears on the next line.'),(1893,12,'What is the purpose of the hr tag?','EASY','A','The hr tag creates a horizontal line.'),(1894,12,'What is the purpose of the iframe tag?','EASY','D','The iframe tag is used to add a different webpage into the current webpage.'),(1895,12,'Which attribute specifies the webpage path in an iframe?','EASY','B','The src attribute specifies the path of the webpage to be embedded.'),(1896,12,'Which type of YouTube or map link should be used inside an iframe according to the notes?','MEDIUM','C','The notes specify that an embed link should be used for a YouTube video or map.'),(1897,12,'Which HTML tag is used to add audio to a webpage?','EASY','A','The audio tag is used to add audio to a webpage.'),(1898,12,'Which attribute makes audio controls visible on a webpage?','EASY','C','The controls attribute makes the audio player controls visible.'),(1899,12,'Which audio attribute plays the audio repeatedly?','EASY','B','The loop attribute makes the audio play repeatedly.'),(1900,12,'What is the purpose of the autoplay attribute in audio?','EASY','D','Autoplay starts playing audio whenever the webpage reloads, according to the notes.'),(1901,12,'Which attribute makes audio muted by default?','EASY','A','The muted attribute makes the audio muted by default.'),(1902,12,'Which HTML tag is used to add a video to a webpage?','EASY','C','The video tag is used to add video content to a webpage.'),(1903,12,'Which video attribute provides an image to display for the video?','MEDIUM','B','The poster attribute provides an image for the video.'),(1904,12,'Which attributes can be used to resize a video?','EASY','D','The height and width attributes are used to resize the video.'),(1905,12,'Which HTML tag creates a table?','EASY','A','The table tag creates an HTML table.'),(1906,12,'Which tag is used to create a row in an HTML table?','EASY','C','The tr tag creates a table row.'),(1907,12,'Which tags are used to provide data inside an HTML table row?','EASY','B','The th and td tags provide data inside a table row.'),(1908,12,'Which HTML table tag provides a title for the table?','EASY','D','The caption tag provides the title of the table.'),(1909,12,'What is the purpose of the cellspacing attribute?','MEDIUM','A','Cellspacing specifies the space between table cells, outside the cell.'),(1910,12,'What is the purpose of the cellpadding attribute?','MEDIUM','C','Cellpadding specifies the space inside a cell between its content and border.'),(1911,12,'Which attribute combines two or more rows in a table?','EASY','B','Rowspan combines two or more rows.'),(1912,12,'Which attribute combines two or more columns in a table?','EASY','D','Colspan combines two or more columns.'),(1913,12,'Which of the following are semantic table tags mentioned in the notes?','MEDIUM','A','The thead, tbody and tfoot tags are semantic table tags.'),(1914,12,'What does the div tag stand for?','EASY','C','Div stands for division.'),(1915,12,'Which type of HTML element is div?','EASY','B','The div element is a block-level element.'),(1916,12,'What is the main purpose of the div tag?','MEDIUM','D','Div is a container used to group elements for styling and layout purposes.'),(1917,12,'Which type of element is the span tag?','EASY','B','Span is an inline-level container used to group text or other inline elements.'),(1918,12,'Which statement correctly describes the difference between div and span?','MEDIUM','C','Div groups larger sections and is block-level; span styles smaller inline content.'),(1919,12,'Why is the span tag commonly used inside a paragraph?','MEDIUM','A','Span is used to style or modify a small part of inline content without affecting the overall layout.'),(1920,12,'What is the main purpose of HTML forms?','EASY','D','Forms are used to collect information from users.'),(1921,12,'Which type of element is the form tag according to the notes?','EASY','B','The form tag is a block-level element.'),(1922,12,'Which form attribute specifies the URL where form data will be submitted?','MEDIUM','A','The action attribute specifies the URL where form data will be submitted.'),(1923,12,'Which form attribute specifies how data is sent to the server?','MEDIUM','C','The method attribute specifies how data is sent, using GET or POST according to the notes.'),(1924,12,'Which attribute controls whether form input autocomplete is enabled or disabled?','MEDIUM','D','The autocomplete attribute defines whether autocomplete is enabled or disabled.'),(1925,12,'How is a label linked to an input element?','MEDIUM','B','The label for attribute must match the id of the input element.'),(1926,12,'Which HTML tag is used to collect user data through different input types?','EASY','C','The input tag is used to collect user data.'),(1927,12,'Which tag creates a dropdown list?','EASY','A','The select tag creates a dropdown list, and option defines its choices.'),(1928,12,'Which tag defines individual choices inside a dropdown list?','EASY','D','The option tag defines the choices inside a select element.'),(1929,12,'What is the purpose of the fieldset tag?','MEDIUM','B','Fieldset groups form elements together and provides a border around them.'),(1930,12,'Which tag provides a caption for a fieldset group?','EASY','C','The legend tag provides a caption for the fieldset group.'),(1931,12,'Which tag collects multiline text input?','EASY','A','Textarea collects multiline text input. Rows and cols specify its visible height and width.'),(1932,12,'Which input attribute makes a field mandatory before form submission?','EASY','D','The required attribute makes the field mandatory to fill before submission.'),(1933,12,'Which input attribute prevents the user from modifying the value?','MEDIUM','B','The readonly attribute prevents the user from modifying the value.'),(1934,12,'Which input type allows a user to select one option from a group?','EASY','C','The radio input type is used to select one option from a group.'),(1935,12,'Which input type allows users to select multiple options independently?','EASY','A','The checkbox input type allows multiple options to be selected independently.'),(1936,12,'How do you make radio buttons work as one group according to the notes?','MEDIUM','D','Radio buttons are grouped by giving them the same name attribute.'),(1937,12,'Which input type is used to enter an email address?','EASY','B','The email input type is used for email input and automatically validates the email format according to the notes.'),(1938,12,'Which input type displays entered characters as masked characters?','EASY','C','The password input type displays input as dots or asterisks.'),(1939,12,'Which input type is used to upload files from a device?','EASY','A','The file input type allows users to upload files from their device.'),(1940,12,'Which input type creates a slider to select a numeric value within a range?','EASY','D','The range input type creates a slider for selecting a numeric value within a range.'),(1941,12,'Which input type resets all form fields to their default values?','EASY','B','The reset input type resets all form fields to their default values.'),(1942,12,'Which input type is used to select a date using a date picker?','EASY','C','The date input type allows users to select a date using a date picker.'),(1943,12,'Which input type is used to select a color?','EASY','A','The color input type provides a color picker.'),(1944,12,'Which input type creates a submit button in the form of an image?','MEDIUM','D','The image input type creates a submit button in the form of an image and uses src and alt attributes.'),(1945,12,'Which input attribute associates a name with a field for form submission?','MEDIUM','B','The name attribute associates a name with the input field for form submission.'),(1946,12,'Which input attribute defines the initial value of an input field?','EASY','C','The value attribute defines the initial value of the input field.'),(1947,12,'Which input attribute displays a hint inside the input field?','EASY','A','The placeholder attribute displays hint text inside the input field.'),(1948,12,'Which input attribute disables the input field?','EASY','D','The disabled attribute disables the input field.'),(1949,12,'What are semantic HTML tags?','MEDIUM','B','Semantic tags clearly describe their meaning to both the browser and developer.'),(1950,12,'Which of the following is a non-semantic element mentioned in the notes?','EASY','C','The notes identify div and span as non-semantic elements.'),(1951,12,'Which semantic tag represents the introductory section of a webpage?','EASY','A','The header tag represents an introductory section or a group of navigation links.'),(1952,12,'Which semantic tag represents navigation links or menus?','EASY','D','The nav tag represents a section containing navigation links.'),(1953,12,'Which semantic tag represents the main unique content of a webpage?','EASY','B','The main tag contains the main content, excluding headers, footers and sidebars.'),(1954,12,'Which semantic tag is used for an independent piece of content such as a blog post?','MEDIUM','C','The article tag represents independent content that can be distributed or reused.'),(1955,12,'Which semantic tag groups related content into a thematic section?','MEDIUM','A','The section tag groups related content into a thematic section.'),(1956,12,'Which semantic tag is used for supplementary content such as a sidebar?','MEDIUM','D','The aside tag represents supplementary or tangentially related content.'),(1957,14,'What is the full form of CSS?','EASY','Cascading Style Sheets','CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.'),(1958,14,'What is the main purpose of CSS?','EASY','To provide style and arrange HTML elements','CSS is used to provide styling and arrange HTML elements.'),(1959,14,'How many ways are there to apply CSS according to the notes?','EASY','Three','The three ways are inline CSS, internal CSS and external CSS.'),(1960,14,'Which CSS type uses the style attribute inside an HTML tag?','EASY','Inline CSS','Inline CSS is written directly inside an HTML element using the style attribute.'),(1961,14,'Where is internal CSS written?','EASY','Inside the style tag in the head section','Internal CSS is written using the style tag inside the head section of the HTML document.'),(1962,14,'Which HTML tag is used to write internal CSS?','EASY','style','The style tag is used to write internal CSS.'),(1963,14,'Which CSS type is written in a separate CSS file?','EASY','External CSS','External CSS is written in a separate file and linked to the HTML document.'),(1964,14,'Which HTML tag is used to link an external CSS file?','EASY','link','The link tag is used to connect an external CSS file to an HTML document.'),(1965,14,'Which attribute specifies the path of an external CSS file?','EASY','href','The href attribute specifies the path of the external CSS file in the link tag.'),(1966,14,'Which type of CSS has the highest priority according to the notes?','MEDIUM','Inline CSS','The notes state that inline CSS has the highest priority.'),(1967,14,'What happens when internal and external CSS have the same priority?','MEDIUM','The one written at the end is applied','According to the notes, internal and external CSS have the same priority, and whichever comes last is applied.'),(1968,14,'What is a CSS selector?','EASY','It selects HTML elements to apply styles','A selector identifies the HTML elements to which CSS styles should be applied.'),(1969,14,'How many types of CSS selectors are listed in the notes?','EASY','Five','The five types are simple, combinator, pseudo-class, pseudo-element and attribute selectors.'),(1970,14,'Which symbol is used to represent a CSS ID selector?','EASY','#','An ID selector uses the hash symbol followed by the ID name.'),(1971,14,'Which symbol is used to represent a CSS class selector?','EASY','.','A class selector uses a dot followed by the class name.'),(1972,14,'Which CSS selector selects all elements on a page?','EASY','Universal selector','The universal selector uses the asterisk symbol to target all elements.'),(1973,14,'Which symbol is used in a universal selector?','EASY','*','The asterisk symbol represents the universal selector.'),(1974,14,'Which selector is used to apply the same CSS to multiple elements using a common class name?','EASY','Class selector','A class selector allows the same CSS styles to be applied to multiple elements.'),(1975,14,'Which selector uses an HTML element name to select elements?','EASY','Tag name selector','A tag name selector selects elements based on their HTML tag name.'),(1976,14,'Which selector uses a comma to group multiple selectors?','MEDIUM','Group selector','A group selector uses commas to apply the same styles to multiple selectors.'),(1977,14,'What is a combinator selector?','EASY','A selector that combines two or more simple selectors','A combinator selector combines two or more simple selectors.'),(1978,14,'How many types of combinator selectors are mentioned in the notes?','EASY','Four','The four types are descendant, direct child, adjacent sibling and general sibling selectors.'),(1979,14,'Which symbol represents the descendant selector?','EASY','Space','A space between selectors represents the descendant combinator.'),(1980,14,'Which elements are selected by a descendant selector?','MEDIUM','Children, grandchildren and further descendants','A descendant selector targets matching elements at any descendant level.'),(1981,14,'Which symbol represents the direct child selector?','EASY','>','The greater-than symbol represents the direct child combinator.'),(1982,14,'What does a direct child selector select?','MEDIUM','Only directly related child elements','A direct child selector selects only elements that are direct children of the specified parent.'),(1983,14,'Which symbol represents the adjacent sibling selector?','EASY','+','The plus symbol represents the adjacent sibling combinator.'),(1984,14,'What does the adjacent sibling selector select?','MEDIUM','The next element that shares the same parent','The adjacent sibling selector selects the next matching sibling element with the same parent.'),(1985,14,'Which symbol represents the general sibling selector?','EASY','~','The tilde symbol represents the general sibling combinator.'),(1986,14,'What does the general sibling selector select?','MEDIUM','All matching next sibling elements','The general sibling selector targets all matching following sibling elements.'),(1987,14,'Which symbol is used for a CSS pseudo-class?','EASY',':','A single colon is used to represent a pseudo-class selector.'),(1988,14,'Which pseudo-class is used when the mouse pointer is placed over an element?','EASY',':hover','The hover pseudo-class applies when the pointer is over an element.'),(1989,14,'Which pseudo-class is used when an element is being activated?','EASY',':active','The active pseudo-class represents an element while it is being activated.'),(1990,14,'Which pseudo-class selects an element based on its position among siblings?','MEDIUM',':nth-child()','The nth-child pseudo-class selects an element based on its position among sibling elements.'),(1991,14,'Which nth-child expression selects even-positioned elements?','MEDIUM',':nth-child(2n)','The expression 2n selects even-positioned elements.'),(1992,14,'Which nth-child expression selects odd-positioned elements?','MEDIUM',':nth-child(2n+1)','The expression 2n+1 selects odd-positioned elements.'),(1993,14,'Which pseudo-class selects the first child element?','EASY',':first-child','The first-child pseudo-class selects the first child among its siblings.'),(1994,14,'Which pseudo-class applies when an element receives focus?','EASY',':focus','The focus pseudo-class applies when an element receives focus.'),(1995,14,'Which pseudo-class selects the last child element?','EASY',':last-child','The last-child pseudo-class selects the last child among its siblings.'),(1996,14,'Which selector type uses the double-colon notation?','EASY','Pseudo-element selector','Pseudo-element selectors use double-colon notation in the notes.'),(1997,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the first letter of an element?','EASY','::first-letter','The first-letter pseudo-element targets the first letter of an element.'),(1998,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the first line of text?','EASY','::first-line','The first-line pseudo-element targets the first line of an element.'),(1999,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the portion of text selected by the user?','MEDIUM','::selection','The selection pseudo-element targets the portion of an element selected by the user.'),(2000,14,'Which pseudo-element inserts content before an element?','EASY','::before','The before pseudo-element is used to insert content before an element.'),(2001,14,'Which pseudo-element inserts content after an element?','EASY','::after','The after pseudo-element is used to insert content after an element.'),(2002,14,'Which CSS property is used with before and after pseudo-elements to insert content?','MEDIUM','content','The content property is used with before and after pseudo-elements to insert content.'),(2003,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style list markers?','EASY','::marker','The marker pseudo-element is used to style list markers.'),(2004,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style placeholder text?','EASY','::placeholder','The placeholder pseudo-element targets placeholder text.'),(2005,14,'Which selector targets HTML elements based on their attributes?','EASY','Attribute selector','An attribute selector selects elements based on their attributes.'),(2006,14,'Which syntax represents an attribute selector according to the notes?','MEDIUM','tagname[attributename=\"value\"]','The notes show the attribute selector syntax as tagname followed by the attribute name and value inside square brackets.'),(2007,14,'Which symbol is used to enclose an attribute condition in an attribute selector?','EASY','Square brackets []','Attribute selectors use square brackets around the attribute condition.'),(2008,14,'Which notation represents a pseudo-class selector?','EASY',':hover','Pseudo-class selectors use a single colon, as shown by the hover selector.'),(2009,14,'Which notation represents a pseudo-element selector?','EASY','::first-letter','Pseudo-element selectors use double-colon notation.'),(2010,14,'Which of the following is a pseudo-class selector?','EASY',':nth-child()','The nth-child selector is one of the pseudo-classes listed in the notes.'),(2011,14,'Which of the following is a pseudo-element?','EASY','::placeholder','The placeholder selector is listed as a pseudo-element in the notes.'),(2012,14,'Which selector uses a dot followed by a name?','EASY','Class selector','A class selector uses a dot followed by the class name.'),(2013,14,'Which selector uses a hash symbol followed by a name?','EASY','ID selector','An ID selector uses the hash symbol followed by the ID name.'),(2014,14,'According to the notes, should the same ID be assigned to more than one HTML element?','MEDIUM','No','The notes state that the same ID should not be given to more than one element.'),(2015,14,'Which selector groups multiple selectors using commas?','EASY','Group selector','A group selector uses commas to group multiple selectors and apply the same CSS.'),(2016,14,'Which of the following is the correct CSS selector syntax?','MEDIUM','selector { property: value; }','The notes show CSS syntax using a selector followed by curly braces containing properties and their values.'),(2017,12,'A form must collect an email address and validate its email format. Which input type should be used?','MEDIUM','email','The email input type automatically validates the email format according to the notes.'),(2018,12,'A registration form asks the user to select only one gender option. Which input type is suitable?','MEDIUM','radio','Radio buttons are used to select one option from a group.'),(2019,12,'A form allows users to select multiple hobbies independently. Which input type is suitable?','MEDIUM','checkbox','Checkboxes allow users to select multiple options independently.'),(2020,12,'Two radio buttons must work as one group. What should they have in common?','MEDIUM','The same name attribute','According to the notes, radio buttons work as a group when they have the same name attribute.'),(2021,12,'A form should send its data to the URL /submit-data. Which form attribute specifies this URL?','MEDIUM','action','The action attribute specifies the URL where form data will be submitted.'),(2022,12,'A user wants to clear all form fields and restore their default values. Which input type should be used?','EASY','reset','The reset input type resets all form fields to their default values.'),(2023,12,'A developer wants to allow numeric values only within a range of 1 to 100. Which input attributes can be used?','MEDIUM','min and max','The number input type can use min, max and step attributes for validation.'),(2024,12,'A developer wants to group a large section of webpage content for styling. Which HTML element is suitable?','EASY','div','The div element is a block-level container used to group elements for styling and layout.'),(2025,12,'A developer wants to style only a small part of text inside a paragraph without creating a new line. Which element should be used?','MEDIUM','span','Span is an inline-level container used to group or style small parts of inline content.'),(2026,12,'A table cell must combine two columns. Which attribute should be used?','MEDIUM','colspan','The colspan attribute combines two or more columns in a table.'),(2027,14,'You want to apply the same style to multiple paragraphs using a common class named note. Which selector is correct?','MEDIUM','.note','A class selector uses a dot followed by the class name.'),(2028,14,'You want to select all paragraph elements inside a div, including paragraphs nested inside other elements. Which combinator should be used?','MEDIUM','Descendant selector','A descendant selector uses a space and targets descendants at different levels.'),(2029,14,'You want to select only paragraph elements directly inside a div, not nested deeper. Which combinator should be used?','MEDIUM','Direct child selector','The direct child selector uses > and selects only directly related child elements.'),(2030,14,'You want to select the paragraph immediately following an h1, where both have the same parent. Which combinator should be used?','MEDIUM','Adjacent sibling selector','The adjacent sibling selector uses + and selects the next element sharing the same parent.'),(2031,14,'You want to select all following sibling paragraphs after an h1 that share the same parent. Which combinator should be used?','MEDIUM','General sibling selector','The general sibling selector uses ~ and targets all following sibling elements.'),(2032,14,'You want to change the style of an element when the mouse cursor is placed over it. Which pseudo-class should be used?','EASY',':hover','The hover pseudo-class applies when the mouse cursor is placed over an element.'),(2033,14,'You want to style every even list item. Which selector expression is given in the notes?','MEDIUM',':nth-child(2n)','The notes use nth-child(2n) to target even-positioned list items.'),(2034,14,'You want to add three asterisks after an h1 using CSS. Which pseudo-element and property should be used?','MEDIUM','::after with content','The after pseudo-element adds content after the selected element, using the content property.'),(2035,14,'You want to style only the placeholder text inside an input element. Which pseudo-element should be used?','MEDIUM','::placeholder','The placeholder pseudo-element targets placeholder text inside input or textarea elements.'),(2036,14,'You want to select input elements whose type attribute has the value email. Which selector syntax matches the attribute selector format in the notes?','MEDIUM','input[type=\"email\"]','The attribute selector syntax is tagname[attributename=\"value\"].'),(2037,12,'What does HTML stand for?','EASY','B','HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.'),(2038,12,'What is the main purpose of HTML?','EASY','C','HTML is used to create the structure of a webpage.'),(2039,12,'Why is HTML not considered a programming language according to the notes?','EASY','A','HTML does not involve writing logic; it creates webpage structure using tags.'),(2040,12,'What is hypertext?','EASY','D','Any text that contains a link to another webpage is called hypertext.'),(2041,12,'Which tag is the root tag of an HTML document?','EASY','B','The html tag is the root tag and contains the document content.'),(2042,12,'Which section provides information about the HTML document?','EASY','A','The head tag provides information about the HTML document.'),(2043,12,'Which tag defines the document name displayed in the browser tab?','EASY','C','The title tag provides the document name shown in the browser tab.'),(2044,12,'Why is the meta tag described as an unpaired tag in the notes?','MEDIUM','D','The notes describe meta as having only an opening tag.'),(2045,12,'Which tag contains the content displayed on the webpage UI?','EASY','B','The body tag contains the HTML content displayed on the webpage.'),(2046,12,'What does <!DOCTYPE html> indicate according to the notes?','EASY','A','It tells the version of HTML; the notes identify HTML5 as the current version.'),(2047,12,'What are HTML tags?','EASY','C','Tags are predefined words enclosed within angular brackets.'),(2048,12,'What are the two types of HTML tags mentioned in the notes?','EASY','D','The two types are paired tags and unpaired or self-closing tags.'),(2049,12,'Which of the following is an example of an unpaired tag from the notes?','EASY','A','br, hr and meta are listed as unpaired tags.'),(2050,12,'What is an HTML element?','EASY','B','An element is a combination of tags and content.'),(2051,12,'Which three types of elements are listed in the notes?','EASY','C','The notes list inline, block and inline-block level elements.'),(2052,12,'Which statement describes inline-level elements?','MEDIUM','A','Inline elements display 