ning to both the browser and developer.'),(2150,12,'Which of the following is a non-semantic element mentioned in the notes?','EASY','C','The notes identify div and span as non-semantic elements.'),(2151,12,'Which semantic tag represents the introductory section of a webpage?','EASY','A','The header tag represents an introductory section or a group of navigation links.'),(2152,12,'Which semantic tag represents navigation links or menus?','EASY','D','The nav tag represents a section containing navigation links.'),(2153,12,'Which semantic tag represents the main unique content of a webpage?','EASY','B','The main tag contains the main content, excluding headers, footers and sidebars.'),(2154,12,'Which semantic tag is used for an independent piece of content such as a blog post?','MEDIUM','C','The article tag represents independent content that can be distributed or reused.'),(2155,12,'Which semantic tag groups related content into a thematic section?','MEDIUM','A','The section tag groups related content into a thematic section.'),(2156,12,'Which semantic tag is used for supplementary content such as a sidebar?','MEDIUM','D','The aside tag represents supplementary or tangentially related content.'),(2157,14,'What is the full form of CSS?','EASY','Cascading Style Sheets','CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.'),(2158,14,'What is the main purpose of CSS?','EASY','To provide style and arrange HTML elements','CSS is used to provide styling and arrange HTML elements.'),(2159,14,'How many ways are there to apply CSS according to the notes?','EASY','Three','The three ways are inline CSS, internal CSS and external CSS.'),(2160,14,'Which CSS type uses the style attribute inside an HTML tag?','EASY','Inline CSS','Inline CSS is written directly inside an HTML element using the style attribute.'),(2161,14,'Where is internal CSS written?','EASY','Inside the style tag in the head section','Internal CSS is written using the style tag inside the head section of the HTML document.'),(2162,14,'Which HTML tag is used to write internal CSS?','EASY','style','The style tag is used to write internal CSS.'),(2163,14,'Which CSS type is written in a separate CSS file?','EASY','External CSS','External CSS is written in a separate file and linked to the HTML document.'),(2164,14,'Which HTML tag is used to link an external CSS file?','EASY','link','The link tag is used to connect an external CSS file to an HTML document.'),(2165,14,'Which attribute specifies the path of an external CSS file?','EASY','href','The href attribute specifies the path of the external CSS file in the link tag.'),(2166,14,'Which type of CSS has the highest priority according to the notes?','MEDIUM','Inline CSS','The notes state that inline CSS has the highest priority.'),(2167,14,'What happens when internal and external CSS have the same priority?','MEDIUM','The one written at the end is applied','According to the notes, internal and external CSS have the same priority, and whichever comes last is applied.'),(2168,14,'What is a CSS selector?','EASY','It selects HTML elements to apply styles','A selector identifies the HTML elements to which CSS styles should be applied.'),(2169,14,'How many types of CSS selectors are listed in the notes?','EASY','Five','The five types are simple, combinator, pseudo-class, pseudo-element and attribute selectors.'),(2170,14,'Which symbol is used to represent a CSS ID selector?','EASY','#','An ID selector uses the hash symbol followed by the ID name.'),(2171,14,'Which symbol is used to represent a CSS class selector?','EASY','.','A class selector uses a dot followed by the class name.'),(2172,14,'Which CSS selector selects all elements on a page?','EASY','Universal selector','The universal selector uses the asterisk symbol to target all elements.'),(2173,14,'Which symbol is used in a universal selector?','EASY','*','The asterisk symbol represents the universal selector.'),(2174,14,'Which selector is used to apply the same CSS to multiple elements using a common class name?','EASY','Class selector','A class selector allows the same CSS styles to be applied to multiple elements.'),(2175,14,'Which selector uses an HTML element name to select elements?','EASY','Tag name selector','A tag name selector selects elements based on their HTML tag name.'),(2176,14,'Which selector uses a comma to group multiple selectors?','MEDIUM','Group selector','A group selector uses commas to apply the same styles to multiple selectors.'),(2177,14,'What is a combinator selector?','EASY','A selector that combines two or more simple selectors','A combinator selector combines two or more simple selectors.'),(2178,14,'How many types of combinator selectors are mentioned in the notes?','EASY','Four','The four types are descendant, direct child, adjacent sibling and general sibling selectors.'),(2179,14,'Which symbol represents the descendant selector?','EASY','Space','A space between selectors represents the descendant combinator.'),(2180,14,'Which elements are selected by a descendant selector?','MEDIUM','Children, grandchildren and further descendants','A descendant selector targets matching elements at any descendant level.'),(2181,14,'Which symbol represents the direct child selector?','EASY','>','The greater-than symbol represents the direct child combinator.'),(2182,14,'What does a direct child selector select?','MEDIUM','Only directly related child elements','A direct child selector selects only elements that are direct children of the specified parent.'),(2183,14,'Which symbol represents the adjacent sibling selector?','EASY','+','The plus symbol represents the adjacent sibling combinator.'),(2184,14,'What does the adjacent sibling selector select?','MEDIUM','The next element that shares the same parent','The adjacent sibling selector selects the next matching sibling element with the same parent.'),(2185,14,'Which symbol represents the general sibling selector?','EASY','~','The tilde symbol represents the general sibling combinator.'),(2186,14,'What does the general sibling selector select?','MEDIUM','All matching next sibling elements','The general sibling selector targets all matching following sibling elements.'),(2187,14,'Which symbol is used for a CSS pseudo-class?','EASY',':','A single colon is used to represent a pseudo-class selector.'),(2188,14,'Which pseudo-class is used when the mouse pointer is placed over an element?','EASY',':hover','The hover pseudo-class applies when the pointer is over an element.'),(2189,14,'Which pseudo-class is used when an element is being activated?','EASY',':active','The active pseudo-class represents an element while it is being activated.'),(2190,14,'Which pseudo-class selects an element based on its position among siblings?','MEDIUM',':nth-child()','The nth-child pseudo-class selects an element based on its position among sibling elements.'),(2191,14,'Which nth-child expression selects even-positioned elements?','MEDIUM',':nth-child(2n)','The expression 2n selects even-positioned elements.'),(2192,14,'Which nth-child expression selects odd-positioned elements?','MEDIUM',':nth-child(2n+1)','The expression 2n+1 selects odd-positioned elements.'),(2193,14,'Which pseudo-class selects the first child element?','EASY',':first-child','The first-child pseudo-class selects the first child among its siblings.'),(2194,14,'Which pseudo-class applies when an element receives focus?','EASY',':focus','The focus pseudo-class applies when an element receives focus.'),(2195,14,'Which pseudo-class selects the last child element?','EASY',':last-child','The last-child pseudo-class selects the last child among its siblings.'),(2196,14,'Which selector type uses the double-colon notation?','EASY','Pseudo-element selector','Pseudo-element selectors use double-colon notation in the notes.'),(2197,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the first letter of an element?','EASY','::first-letter','The first-letter pseudo-element targets the first letter of an element.'),(2198,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the first line of text?','EASY','::first-line','The first-line pseudo-element targets the first line of an element.'),(2199,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style the portion of text selected by the user?','MEDIUM','::selection','The selection pseudo-element targets the portion of an element selected by the user.'),(2200,14,'Which pseudo-element inserts content before an element?','EASY','::before','The before pseudo-element is used to insert content before an element.'),(2201,14,'Which pseudo-element inserts content after an element?','EASY','::after','The after pseudo-element is used to insert content after an element.'),(2202,14,'Which CSS property is used with before and after pseudo-elements to insert content?','MEDIUM','content','The content property is used with before and after pseudo-elements to insert content.'),(2203,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style list markers?','EASY','::marker','The marker pseudo-element is used to style list markers.'),(2204,14,'Which pseudo-element is used to style placeholder text?','EASY','::placeholder','The placeholder pseudo-element targets placeholder text.'),(2205,14,'Which selector targets HTML elements based on their attributes?','EASY','Attribute selector','An attribute selector selects elements based on their attributes.'),(2206,14,'Which syntax represents an attribute selector according to the notes?','MEDIUM','tagname[attributename=\"value\"]','The notes show the attribute selector syntax as tagname followed by the attribute name and value inside square brackets.'),(2207,14,'Which symbol is used to enclose an attribute condition in an attribute selector?','EASY','Square brackets []','Attribute selectors use square brackets around the attribute condition.'),(2208,14,'Which notation represents a pseudo-class selector?','EASY',':hover','Pseudo-class selectors use a single colon, as shown by the hover selector.'),(2209,14,'Which notation represents a pseudo-element selector?','EASY','::first-letter','Pseudo-element selectors use double-colon notation.'),(2210,14,'Which of the following is a pseudo-class selector?','EASY',':nth-child()','The nth-child selector is one of the pseudo-classes listed in the notes.'),(2211,14,'Which of the following is a pseudo-element?','EASY','::placeholder','The placeholder selector is listed as a pseudo-element in the notes.'),(2212,14,'Which selector uses a dot followed by a name?','EASY','Class selector','A class selector uses a dot followed by the class name.'),(2213,14,'Which selector uses a hash symbol followed by a name?','EASY','ID selector','An ID selector uses the hash symbol followed by the ID name.'),(2214,14,'According to the notes, should the same ID be assigned to more than one HTML element?','MEDIUM','No','The notes state that the same ID should not be given to more than one element.'),(2215,14,'Which selector groups multiple selectors using commas?','EASY','Group selector','A group selector uses commas to group multiple selectors and apply the same CSS.'),(2216,14,'Which of the following is the correct CSS selector syntax?','MEDIUM','selector { property: value; }','The notes show CSS syntax using a selector followed by curly braces containing properties and their values.'),(2217,12,'A form must collect an email address and validate its email format. Which input type should be used?','MEDIUM','email','The email input type automatically validates the email format according to the notes.'),(2218,12,'A registration form asks the user to select only one gender option. Which input type is suitable?','MEDIUM','radio','Radio buttons are used to select one option from a group.'),(2219,12,'A form allows users to select multiple hobbies independently. Which input type is suitable?','MEDIUM','checkbox','Checkboxes allow users to select multiple options independently.'),(2220,12,'Two radio buttons must work as one group. What should they have in common?','MEDIUM','The same name attribute','According to