s and throws an exception object?','HARD','throw','throw is followed by a Throwable object.'),(2554,5,'Can a finally block change a method\'s return result?','HARD','Yes, a return in finally can override an earlier return','A return or thrown exception in finally can override the earlier completion; avoid this pattern.'),(2555,5,'Which is a checked exception?','HARD','FileNotFoundException','FileNotFoundException is a checked IOException subtype.'),(2556,5,'When overriding a method, what is true about checked exceptions?','HARD','The overriding method cannot declare broader checked exceptions','An override may narrow or omit checked exceptions, but cannot broaden them.'),(2557,17,'Which organization originally developed Java?','MEDIUM','Sun Microsystems','Java was originally developed at Sun Microsystems.'),(2558,17,'What was the original name of the Java language project?','MEDIUM','Oak','The language was initially called Oak.'),(2559,17,'Which company acquired Sun Microsystems in 2010?','MEDIUM','Oracle','Oracle completed its acquisition of Sun Microsystems in 2010.'),(2560,17,'What is Java\'s commonly stated design principle for portability?','MEDIUM','Write once, run anywhere','Bytecode can run on compatible JVM implementations.'),(2561,17,'Which component executes Java bytecode?','MEDIUM','JVM','The Java Virtual Machine executes bytecode.'),(2562,17,'Which feature helps Java programs run on different operating systems?','MEDIUM','Platform-independent bytecode and JVMs','The JVM abstracts platform-specific execution.'),(2563,17,'Which Java release introduced lambda expressions as a major language feature?','MEDIUM','Java 8','Lambda expressions arrived in Java 8.'),(2564,17,'Which feature is associated with Java 5?','MEDIUM','Generics','Generics were introduced in Java 5.'),(2565,17,'What does Java\'s garbage collector primarily manage?','MEDIUM','Memory reclamation for unreachable objects','Garbage collection reclaims heap memory for objects no longer reachable.'),(2566,17,'Which statement best describes Java\'s object-oriented approach?','MEDIUM','Programs can organize behavior and state into classes and objects','Classes and objects are central to Java programming.'),(2567,17,'Which project name is associated with the early development of Java at Sun?','HARD','Green Project','The Green Project explored software for consumer electronic devices.'),(2568,17,'Which statement best distinguishes Java source code from bytecode?','HARD','Source is compiled into JVM bytecode','The compiler translates source into class-file bytecode.'),(2569,17,'Which Java release introduced the module system through Project Jigsaw?','HARD','Java 9','The Java Platform Module System was delivered in Java 9.'),(2570,17,'Which feature arrived in Java 16 as a standard language feature?','HARD','Records','Records became a standard feature in Java 16.'),(2571,17,'Which statement about Java\'s platform independence is most accurate?','HARD','Bytecode is portable, but a compatible JVM is required on each platform','Portability depends on a JVM implementation for the target platform.'),(2572,17,'Which feature was introduced as a preview in Java 14 and standardized in Java 16?','HARD','Pattern matching for instanceof','Pattern matching for instanceof was previewed in Java 14 and finalized in Java 16.'),(2573,17,'Which Java feature supports automatic memory management?','HARD','Garbage collection','The garbage collector manages reclamation of unreachable heap objects.'),(2574,17,'Which statement about Java and C++ is correct?','HARD','Java does not support multiple inheritance of classes','Java uses single class inheritance and interfaces for multiple-type inheritance.'),(2575,17,'What is the main purpose of the Java Community Process (JCP)?','HARD','Develop and review Java specifications','The JCP is a formal process for developing Java technology specifications.'),(2576,17,'Which statement about Java\'s security model is most accurate?','HARD','It includes language, runtime and platform security mechanisms','Java provides security mechanisms, but applications still require secure design.'),(2577,18,'Which tool converts Java source code into bytecode?','HARD','javac','javac is the Java compiler.'),(2578,18,'Which command launches a compiled Java class?','HARD','java','The java launcher starts the JVM and runs the class.'),(2579,18,'Which component contains the JVM and standard runtime libraries needed to run Java applications?','HARD','JRE','The JRE conceptually includes the JVM and runtime libraries.'),(2580,18,'Which package provides development tools such as the Java compiler?','HARD','JDK','The JDK provides tools for developing Java applications.'),(2581,18,'What is the role of the bytecode verifier?','HARD','Checks class-file bytecode for structural and safety constraints','The verifier checks bytecode validity before execution.'),(2582,18,'Which JVM subsystem loads classes into memory?','HARD','Class Loader','The class-loading subsystem loads class definitions.'),(2583,18,'What does the JIT compiler do?','HARD','Compiles frequently executed bytecode into native machine code','JIT compilation optimizes execution by compiling hot code paths.'),(2584,18,'Which file extension is normally produced by javac?','HARD','class','javac normally generates .class files.'),(2585,18,'Which tool can create a custom runtime image containing selected modules?','HARD','jlink','jlink assembles a custom runtime image.'),(2586,18,'Which statement about JVM implementations is correct?','HARD','Different operating systems can have JVM implementations that execute the same bytecode','JVM implementations are platform-specific while class-file bytecode is portable.'),(2587,23,'What is the output of `for(int i=0;i<3;i++) System.out.print(i);`?','HARD','012','The loop prints 0, 1 and 2.'),(2588,23,'Which loop is guaranteed to execute its body at least once?','HARD','do-while','The do-while condition is checked after the body.'),(2589,23,'What does `continue` do inside a loop?','HARD','Skips the rest of the current iteration','continue advances to the next iteration.'),(2590,23,'What does an unlabeled `break` exit?','HARD','The innermost enclosing loop or switch','An unlabeled break exits the nearest loop or switch.'),(2591,23,'How many times does `for(int i=5;i>5;i--)` execute?','HARD','Zero','The initial condition is false.'),(2592,23,'What is the purpose of a labeled break?','HARD','Exits the statement associated with the label','A labeled break can exit an enclosing labeled loop or block.'),(2593,23,'What happens in `while(true)` if there is no reachable exit?','HARD','The loop continues indefinitely','A constant true condition creates an infinite loop unless exited.'),(2594,23,'In a nested loop, which loop is affected by an unlabeled continue?','HARD','The innermost loop containing it','Unlabeled continue applies to the nearest enclosing loop.'),(2595,23,'What is the value of `sum` after `int sum=0; for(int i=1;i<=4;i++) sum+=i;`?','HARD','10','The sum is 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10.'),(2596,23,'Which expression is evaluated after each iteration in a traditional for loop?','HARD','Update expression','The update expression runs after the body before the next condition check.'),(2597,24,'Which elements are part of a Java method signature?','HARD','Method name and parameter types','The signature consists of the method name and parameter types.'),(2598,24,'Can Java overload methods by changing only the return type?','HARD','No','Return type alone does not distinguish overloaded methods.'),(2599,24,'What is method overriding?','HARD','A subclass provides an implementation matching an inherited instance method','Overriding replaces inherited behavior for a compatible instance method.'),(2600,24,'Which keyword prevents a method from being overridden?','HARD','final','A final method cannot be overridden.'),(2601,24,'What does a varargs parameter allow?','HARD','A method to accept zero or more arguments of a specified type','Varargs are treated as an array parameter inside the method.'),(2602,24,'Where must a varargs parameter appear in a method parameter list?','HARD','Last','Only one varargs parameter is allowed and it must be last.'),(2603,24,'What happens when a method returns from inside a try block with a finally block present?','HARD','The finally block normally executes before the return completes','finally normally executes during method completion.'),(2604,24,'Which statement about static methods is correct?','HARD','They are associated with the class rather than an instance','Static methods belong to the class and cannot use this.'),(2605,24,'What is recursion?','HARD','A method calling itself directly or indirectly','Recursion occurs when a method invokes itself directly or through another method.'),(2606,24,'Which return type is used when a method returns no value?','HARD','void','void indicates that a method does not return a value.'),(2607,21,'What is the result of `10 / 3` when both operands are int?','HARD','3','Integer division truncates the fractional part.'),(2608,21,'What is the result of `10 % 3`?','HARD','1','The remainder operator returns 1.'),(2609,21,'Which operator uses short-circuit evaluation with logical OR?','HARD','||','|| does not evaluate the right operand when the left operand is true.'),(2610,21,'What is the value of `true || (10 / 0 > 1)`?','HARD','true','The right operand is skipped because the left operand is true.'),(2611,21,'Which operator has higher precedence?','HARD','*','Multiplication has higher precedence than addition, shifts and equality.'),(2612,21,'What is the result of `5 & 3` using integer bitwise AND?','HARD','1','0101 AND 0011 equals 0001.'),(2613,21,'Which operator is the conditional ternary operator?','HARD','?:','The conditional operator selects one of two expressions.'),(2614,21,'What is the result of `1 << 3`?','HARD','8','Left shift by three positions multiplies 1 by 8.'),(2615,21,'What does `instanceof` test?','HARD','Whether an object is compatible with a specified type','instanceof performs a runtime type compatibility check.'),(2616,21,'What is the value of `x` after `int x=4; x += 3 * 2;`?','HARD','10','Multiplication occurs first, then compound addition.'),(2617,34,'Which statement declares a package for a Java source file?','HARD','package com.example;','The package declaration identifies the package of the compilation unit.'),(2618,34,'Where must a package declaration appear in a compilation unit?','HARD','Before import declarations and type declarations','A package declaration, if present, is the first non-comment statement.'),(2619,34,'Which command compiles a class in package `com.demo` when source folders are arranged conventionally?','HARD','javac -d . Demo.java','javac -d writes class files into the package directory structure.'),(2620,34,'What does an import declaration do?','HARD','Allows types to be referred to by simple names','Imports affect name resolution, not physical copying or eager loading.'),(2621,34,'Which package is imported automatically into every Java source file?','HARD','java.lang','Types in java.lang are available without an explicit import.'),(2622,34,'Can two packages contain classes with the same simple name?','HARD','Yes','Fully qualified names distinguish types with the same simple name.'),(2623,34,'What is the fully qualified name of class `List` in `java.util`?','HARD','java.util.List','A fully qualified name includes the package and type name.'),(2624,34,'Which statement about wildcard imports is correct?','HARD','`import java.util.*;` imports accessible types in that package, not its subpackages','A package wildcard does not include subpackages.'),(2625,34,'What is the default package?','HARD','A package used by classes with no package declaration','Classes without a package declaration belong to the unnamed/default package.'),(2626,34,'Which access level allows access from classes in the same package without requiring inheritance?','HARD','Package-private','Package-private members are accessible to other classes in the same package.'),(2627,22,'Which method reads an entire line of input using Scanner?','HARD','nextLine()','nextLine reads the remainder of the current line.'),(2628,22,'After calling nextInt(), why might a following nextLine() return an empty string?','HARD','nextInt leaves the line separator in the input buffer','Consume the remaining newline before reading the next full line.'),(2629,22,'Which Scanner method checks whether another token is available?','HARD','hasNext()','hasNext checks for another token.'),(2630,22,'Which statement exits a switch statement?','HARD','break','break exits the switch; return exits the method.'),(2631,22,'Which switch label form is used for a default branch?','HARD','default:','default handles values not matched by other labels.'),(2632,22,'What is the result if no case matches and there is no default label in a traditional switch?','HARD','No case body executes','Without a matching case or default, no switch statement group executes.'),(2633,22,'Which data types can be used in a traditional switch selector?','HARD','byte, short, char, int, their wrappers, enum and String','Java switch supports integral types (except long), wrappers, enums and String.'),(2634,22,'What does `Scanner.nextInt()` do if the next token is not a valid integer?','HARD','Throws InputMismatchException','An invalid token causes InputMismatchException.'),(2635,22,'Which control structure is best for choosing among multiple mutually exclusive branches based on one expression?','HARD','switch','switch selects a matching case based on the selector value.'),(2636,22,'What is the purpose of `default` in a switch?','HARD','Provides a branch when no case label matches','default is the fallback branch.'),(2637,19,'Which of these is a Java keyword?','MEDIUM','class','class is reserved by the Java language.'),(2638,19,'Which is a valid identifier?','MEDIUM','totalMarks','Identifiers cannot start with a digit or contain a hyphen, and keywords are reserved.'),(2639,19,'Which primitive type stores a single 16-bit Unicode character?','MEDIUM','char','char is a 16-bit unsigned integral type representing a UTF-16 code unit.'),(2640,19,'Which primitive type has the widest range among these integral types?','MEDIUM','long','long is a 64-bit signed integral type.'),(2641,19,'Which suffix commonly marks a long integer literal?','MEDIUM','L','The L suffix denotes a long literal.'),(2642,19,'Which literal represents a boolean value?','MEDIUM','true','Java boolean literals are true and false in lowercase.'),(2643,19,'Which is not a primitive type?','MEDIUM','String','String is a reference type.'),(2644,19,'What is the size of an int in Java?','MEDIUM','32 bits','int is a 32-bit signed integer.'),(2645,19,'Which token separates a type from a variable declaration?','MEDIUM','Whitespace','Whitespace separates tokens in declarations such as int count.'),(2646,19,'Which of these is a floating-point primitive type?','MEDIUM','double','double is a 64-bit floating-point primitive.'),(2647,19,'What is the result type of the expression `byteValue + byteValue` when both operands are byte?','HARD','int','Binary numeric promotion promotes byte operands to int.'),(2648,19,'Which statement about `char` arithmetic is correct?','HARD','A char is promoted to int in arithmetic expressions','Numeric promotion converts char to int in arithmetic.'),(2649,19,'Which literal is a valid hexadecimal integer literal?','HARD','0x2A','Java hexadecimal integer literals use the 0x or 0X prefix.'),(2650,19,'What is the type of the literal `3.0` by default?','HARD','double','A decimal floating-point literal without F or f is double.'),(2651,19,'Which statement about Java identifiers is true?','HARD','They are case-sensitive','Java identifiers distinguish uppercase and lowercase letters.'),(2652,19,'What is the result of assigning an int variable to a byte without a cast when the value is not a constant expression?','HARD','Compilation error','Narrowing primitive conversions require an explicit cast, subject to constant-expression rules.'),(2653,19,'Which escape sequence represents a tab character?','HARD','\\t','The escape sequence \\t represents a horizontal tab.'),(2654,19,'Which statement about `var` local-variable inference is correct?','HARD','The compiler infers the local variable\'s type from its initializer','var is compile-time local-variable type inference and requires an initializer.'),(2655,19,'Which type can represent the value 3.5 without an explicit cast?','HARD','double','3.5 is a double literal and fits in a double variable.'),(2656,19,'Which of the following is a valid Java comment token?','HARD','//','// begins a single-line Java comment.'),(2657,20,'What happens when a double value is cast to int?','HARD','The fractional part is discarded toward zero','Floating-point to integer conversion truncates toward zero.'),(2658,20,'Which conversion is a widening primitive conversion?','HARD','int to long','Widening from int to long preserves the value.'),(2659,20,'Which conversion requires an explicit cast?','HARD','double to int','double to int is narrowing.'),(2660,20,'What is the default value of an instance variable of type boolean?','HARD','false','Boolean instance fields default to false.'),(2661,20,'What is the default value of an instance variable of a reference type?','HARD','null','Reference fields default to null.'),(2662,20,'Which variable must be initialized before it is read?','HARD','Local variable','Local variables do not receive automatic default values.'),(2663,20,'What does the final keyword mean for a local primitive variable?','HARD','It can be assigned only once','A final local variable may be assigned once and cannot be reassigned.'),(2664,20,'What is the result of `(int) -3.9`?','HARD','-3','Casting truncates toward zero, producing -3.'),(2665,20,'Which statement about reference casting is correct?','HARD','A downcast may fail at runtime with ClassCastException','A downcast is checked at runtime.'),(2666,20,'What is variable shadowing?','HARD','A local variable uses the same name as a field and hides it in its scope','A local declaration can shadow a field; this can be disambiguated with this.field.'),(2667,12,'Which HTML element is used to associate a text label with a form control?','HARD','label','The label element associates descriptive text with a form control, commonly using the for attribute.'),(2668,12,'Which attribute provides alternative text for an image?','HARD','alt','The alt attribute provides a text alternative for an image.'),(2669,12,'Which element represents the main content unique to a document?','HARD','main','The main element represents the dominant content of the body.'),(2670,12,'Which element is appropriate for a self-contained composition that could be independently distributed?','HARD','article','An article is intended for independently reusable or distributable content.'),(2671,12,'Which attribute makes a form control mandatory before submission?','HARD','required','The required attribute prevents submission until the control has a value.'),(2672,12,'Which element is used to provide a caption for a figure?','HARD','figcaption','figcaption provides a caption for its parent figure.'),(2673,12,'Which attribute on a script element defers execution until after HTML parsing?','HARD','defer','defer downloads the script in parallel and executes it after parsing, preserving order among deferred scripts.'),(2674,12,'Which element should contain metadata such as the document title and linked stylesheets?','HARD','head','The head element contains document metadata and resource links.'),(2675,12,'Which attribute specifies that an input must match a regular expression?','HARD','pattern','The pattern attribute provides a regular expression constraint for supported input types.'),(2676,12,'Which element is used to group related controls in a form with a shared caption?','HARD','fieldset','fieldset groups related form controls and can use legend as its caption.'),(2677,14,'Which CSS property controls the stacking order of positioned elements?','HARD','z-index','z-index controls the stacking level of positioned elements and certain flex/grid items.'),(2678,14,'In the CSS box model, what is the space between content and border?','HARD','padding','Padding is the inner space between content and the border.'),(2679,14,'Which selector has the highest specificity?','HARD','An ID selector','An ID selector has greater specificity than class and element selectors.'),(2680,14,'Which declaration makes an element a flex container?','HARD','display: flex;','display:flex establishes a flex formatting context for the element\'s children.'),(2681,14,'Which property controls whether content overflowing an element is clipped or scrollable?','HARD','overflow','The overflow property controls content that exceeds an element\'s box.'),(2682,14,'What does `box-sizing: border-box` do?','HARD','Includes padding and border in the declared width and height','With border-box, the specified dimensions include content, padding and border.'),(2683,14,'Which pseudo-class selects an element when the user points at it with a pointing device?','HARD',':hover',':hover applies while the pointing device designates the element.'),(2684,14,'Which CSS unit is relative to the font size of the root element?','HARD','rem','rem is relative to the root element\'s font size.'),(2685,14,'Which property defines the columns in a CSS Grid container?','HARD','grid-template-columns','grid-template-columns specifies the size and number of explicit grid columns.'),(2686,14,'Which declaration prevents a flex item from shrinking below its content-based minimum size?','HARD','min-width: 0;','Setting min-width:0 allows a flex item to shrink below its automatic min-content minimum when appropriate.'),(2687,5,'Which keyword is used to handle an exception?','MEDIUM','catch','A catch block handles an exception thrown from its associated try block.'),(2688,6,'Which method releases a thread\'s monitor lock while waiting for a condition?','HARD','wait()','Object.wait releases the object\'s monitor while the thread waits.'),(2689,6,'Which method must be called by a thread to request monitor ownership before entering a synchronized block?','HARD','It must acquire the monitor by entering the synchronized block','The JVM obtains the monitor when execution enters a synchronized region.'),(2690,6,'What is the main purpose of the volatile keyword?','HARD','To make reads and writes visible across threads with ordering guarantees','volatile provides visibility and ordering guarantees, but does not make compound updates atomic.'),(2691,6,'Which interface represents a task whose call() method can return a result?','HARD','Callable','Callable.call returns a value and may throw checked exceptions.'),(2692,17,'Which language was Java originally designed to resemble in syntax?','EASY','C and C++','Java syntax was influenced by C and C++.'),(2693,17,'What is the extension of a Java source file?','EASY','.java','Java source files conventionally use the .java extension.'),(2694,17,'Which feature allows Java code to run on different operating systems through a JVM?','EASY','Platform independence','Java bytecode can run on compatible JVM implementations.'),(2695,18,'What does JVM stand for?','EASY','Java Virtual Machine','JVM stands for Java Virtual Machine.'),(2696,18,'Which file usually contains Java bytecode?','EASY','A .class file','Compiled Java bytecode is stored in class files.'),(2697,18,'Which command is commonly used to compile a Java source file?','EASY','javac','javac compiles source code into bytecode.'),(2698,18,'Which command runs a compiled Java class?','EASY','java','The java launcher starts the JVM to run the class.'),(2699,18,'Which component manages execution of Java bytecode?','EASY','JVM','The JVM loads and executes Java bytecode.'),(2700,18,'Which component provides tools for developing Java programs?','EASY','JDK','The JDK includes development tools such as the compiler.'),(2701,18,'Which tool generates API documentation from Java source comments?','MEDIUM','javadoc','javadoc generates HTML API documentation.'),(2702,18,'Which tool disassembles class files and displays bytecode?','MEDIUM','javap','javap is the class-file disassembler.'),(2703,18,'What is the role of the class loader?','MEDIUM','Loads class definitions into the JVM','Class loaders locate and load class definitions.'),(2704,18,'Which JVM component performs automatic memory reclamation?','MEDIUM','Garbage collector','The garbage collector reclaims memory occupied by unreachable objects.'),(2705,18,'What does the bytecode verifier check?','MEDIUM','Whether bytecode satisfies structural and type-safety constraints','Verification checks class-file bytecode before execution.'),(2706,18,'What is the purpose of the JIT compiler?','MEDIUM','To compile frequently executed bytecode into native machine code','JIT compilation optimizes frequently executed code paths.'),(2707,18,'Which part of the Java platform contains the compiler?','MEDIUM','JDK','The compiler is a JDK development tool.'),(2708,18,'What does a Java runtime environment provide conceptually?','MEDIUM','The JVM and libraries needed to run Java applications','The runtime environment supplies the JVM and runtime libraries.'),(2709,18,'Which command packages compiled classes into a JAR archive?','MEDIUM','jar','The jar tool creates and manipulates JAR archives.'),(2710,19,'Which primitive type stores whole numbers and uses 32 bits?','EASY','int','int is a 32-bit signed integral primitive.'),(2711,19,'Which primitive type stores true or false?','EASY','boolean','boolean represents true or false.'),(2712,19,'Which primitive type stores a 64-bit floating-point value?','EASY','double','double is the 64-bit floating-point primitive.'),(2713,20,'Which keyword declares a constant-like variable that cannot be reassigned?','EASY','final','A final variable can be assigned once.'),(2714,20,'Which kind of variable is declared inside a method?','EASY','Local variable','A variable declared within a method is local to that method or block.'),(2715,20,'Which operator assigns a value to a variable?','EASY','=','The assignment operator stores the right-hand value in the left-hand variable.'),(2716,20,'What is the default value of an int instance field?','EASY','0','Numeric instance fields of integral types default to zero.'),(2717,20,'Which keyword declares a class-level variable shared by instances?','EASY','static','A static field belongs to the class rather than each instance.'),(2718,20,'Which keyword refers to the current object?','EASY','this','this refers to the current instance.'),(2719,20,'Which conversion happens automatically when assigning an int value to a long variable?','MEDIUM','Widening conversion','An int-to-long conversion widens the primitive value.'),(2720,20,'Which cast is required to assign a double expression to an int variable?','MEDIUM','(int)','Converting double to int is a narrowing conversion and needs an explicit cast.'),(2721,20,'What is variable scope?','MEDIUM','The region of code where a variable can be accessed','Scope determines where a variable name is visible.'),(2722,20,'What is the result of casting 8.9 to int?','MEDIUM','8','Casting a floating-point value to an integer truncates toward zero.'),(2723,20,'Which declaration creates an instance variable?','MEDIUM','A field declared inside a class but outside methods','Instance fields belong to each object.'),(2724,20,'Which keyword can prevent a method parameter from being reassigned within the method?','MEDIUM','final','A final parameter cannot be reassigned after initialization.'),(2725,20,'What does explicit casting do?','MEDIUM','Requests a conversion from one type to another','A cast explicitly requests a type conversion, subject to conversion rules.'),(2726,21,'Which operator checks whether two primitive values are equal?','EASY','==','== compares primitive values for equality.'),(2727,21,'Which operator means logical AND?','EASY','&&','&& returns true when both boolean operands are true.'),(2728,21,'Which operator increments a numeric variable by one?','EASY','++','The increment operator increases its operand by one.'),(2729,21,'What is the value of 7 / 2 when both operands are int?','MEDIUM','3','Integer division discards the fractional part.'),(2730,21,'Which operator is used for logical NOT?','MEDIUM','!','! reverses a boolean value.'),(2731,21,'What does the expression `x += 5` mean?','MEDIUM','x = x + 5','The compound assignment adds five to x and stores the result.'),(2732,21,'Which operator returns the remainder after division?','MEDIUM','%','The remainder operator is percent.'),(2733,21,'Which operator compares whether one value is greater than another? ','MEDIUM','>','The greater-than operator returns true when its left operand is larger.'),(2734,21,'Which operator is used to choose between two expressions based on a condition?','MEDIUM','?:','The ternary conditional operator selects one of two expressions.'),(2735,21,'What is the result of `true && false`?','MEDIUM','false','Logical AND is true only when both operands are true.'),(2736,21,'Which operator performs bitwise OR on integer operands?','MEDIUM','|','A single vertical bar performs bitwise OR on integral operands.'),(2737,21,'What does `i++` do when used as an expression?','MEDIUM','Yields the old value, then increments i','Post-increment evaluates to the old value before updating the variable.'),(2738,22,'Which Scanner method reads an integer token?','EASY','nextInt()','nextInt reads the next token as an integer.'),(2739,22,'Which keyword starts a conditional statement?','EASY','if','if begins a conditional branch.'),(2740,22,'Which keyword provides an alternative branch after if?','EASY','else','else runs when the if condition is false.'),(2741,22,'Which statement selects among multiple cases?','EASY','switch','switch selects a branch based on a selector value.'),(2742,22,'Which Scanner method reads a complete line of text?','MEDIUM','nextLine()','nextLine reads the remainder of the current line.'),(2743,22,'Which loop is most suitable when the number of iterations is known?','MEDIUM','for','A for loop conveniently combines initialization, condition and update.'),(2744,22,'What does break do inside a loop?','MEDIUM','Terminates the nearest enclosing loop','break exits the nearest enclosing loop.'),(2745,22,'What does continue do inside a loop?','MEDIUM','Skips to the next iteration','continue skips the rest of the current iteration.'),(2746,22,'Which Scanner method checks whether the next token can be read as an integer?','MEDIUM','hasNextInt()','hasNextInt checks the next token without consuming it.'),(2747,22,'Which structure executes its body at least once?','MEDIUM','do-while','A do-while checks its condition after executing the body.'),(2748,22,'What happens when an if condition evaluates to false and there is no else block?','MEDIUM','The if body is skipped','The statements in the if body are not executed.'),(2749,23,'Which keyword begins a while loop?','EASY','while','while introduces a condition-controlled loop.'),(2750,23,'Which part of a for loop is checked before each iteration?','EASY','Condition','The condition determines whether the next iteration runs.'),(2751,23,'Which loop is commonly used to iterate through an array\'s elements?','EASY','Enhanced for loop','The enhanced for loop visits each element in an array or iterable.'),(2752,23,'Which keyword exits a loop immediately?','EASY','break','break terminates the nearest enclosing loop.'),(2753,23,'Which loop checks its condition after executing its body?','EASY','do-while','do-while evaluates the condition after the loop body.'),(2754,23,'How many times does `for(int i=0; i<4; i++)` execute?','MEDIUM','4','The values 0, 1, 2 and 3 satisfy the condition.'),(2755,23,'What happens if the condition of a while loop is false initially?','MEDIUM','The body executes zero times','A while loop checks its condition before entering the body.'),(2756,23,'Which statement skips the remaining statements in the current iteration?','MEDIUM','continue','continue moves control to the next iteration.'),(2757,23,'What is an infinite loop?','MEDIUM','A loop whose termination condition is never reached','An infinite loop continues until an external or explicit exit occurs.'),(2758,23,'Which loop syntax is valid for iterating over an int array named nums?','MEDIUM','for (int n : nums)','Java enhanced for uses a variable declaration, colon and array or iterable.'),(2759,23,'What does a nested loop mean?','MEDIUM','A loop placed inside another loop','A nested loop is contained within another loop.'),(2760,23,'How many times does the inner loop run in total when an outer loop runs 3 times and an inner loop runs 2 times per outer iteration?','MEDIUM','6','The inner body executes 3 multiplied by 2 times.'),(2761,24,'Which keyword is used to send a value back from a method?','EASY','return','return exits the method and can provide a value.'),(2762,24,'Which part of a method declaration specifies the value type returned?','EASY','Return type','The return type appears before the method name.'),(2763,24,'What is a method parameter?','EASY','A variable listed in a method declaration','Parameters receive argument values when a method is called.'),(2764,24,'Which keyword declares a method that belongs to the class?','EASY','static','A static method is associated with the class.'),(2765,24,'Can a Java method have zero parameters?','EASY','Yes','Methods may declare no parameters.'),(2766,24,'What is method overloading?','MEDIUM','Defining methods with the same name but different parameter lists','Overloaded methods differ in their parameter lists.'),(2767,24,'What is the return type of a method that returns no value?','MEDIUM','void','void indicates that no value is returned.'),(2768,24,'What is an argument in a method call?','MEDIUM','The value passed to a parameter','Arguments are supplied when invoking a method.'),(2769,24,'Which keyword refers to the parent class?','MEDIUM','super','super refers to the superclass portion of the current object.'),(2770,24,'Which method signature is a valid overload of `show(int x)`?','MEDIUM','show(String x)','Changing the parameter type creates a distinct overload.'),(2771,24,'What is recursion?','MEDIUM','A method calling itself','A recursive method invokes itself directly or indirectly.'),(2772,24,'Which statement about Java argument passing is correct?','MEDIUM','Java passes arguments by value','Java passes a copy of the value, including a copied object reference.'),(2773,34,'Which keyword is used to declare a package?','EASY','package','The package keyword declares the package for a source file.'),(2774,34,'Which keyword allows a type from another package to be used by its simple name?','EASY','import','import allows types to be referred to by simple names.'),(2775,34,'Which package contains the String class?','EASY','java.lang','String belongs to java.lang.'),(2776,34,'Which package contains ArrayList?','EASY','java.util','ArrayList is in java.util.'),(2777,34,'What is the purpose of packages in Java?','EASY','Organize related classes and interfaces','Packages organize types and help manage namespaces and access.'),(2778,34,'Which package is imported automatically in Java source files?','MEDIUM','java.lang','Types in java.lang are available without an explicit import.'),(2779,34,'What is a fully qualified class name?','MEDIUM','The package name followed by the class name','A fully qualified name identifies a type using its package and type name.'),(2780,34,'Can two packages contain classes with the same simple name?','MEDIUM','Yes, their fully qualified names distinguish them','Package qualification distinguishes same-named types.'),(2781,34,'Does `import java.util.*;` import classes from `java.util.concurrent`?','MEDIUM','No','A wildcard import applies to the named package, not its subpackages.'),(2782,34,'Where should the package declaration appear in a source file?','MEDIUM','Before import declarations and type declarations','The package declaration appears first, apart from comments.'),(2783,35,'Which access modifier allows a member to be used only inside its declaring class?','EASY','private','private restricts access to the declaring top-level class.'),(2784,35,'Which access modifier makes a class member accessible from any package?','EASY','public','A public member can be accessed wherever its declaring type is accessible.'),(2785,35,'What is the access level when no modifier is written on a class member?','EASY','Package-private','No modifier gives package-private access.'),(2786,35,'Which access modifier is used for a member accessible in the same package and by subclasses?','EASY','protected','protected allows same-package access and subclass access.'),(2787,35,'Which modifier is not allowed on a top-level class?','EASY','private','Top-level classes can be public or package-private, not private.'),(2788,35,'Can a private method be overridden by a subclass?','MEDIUM','No, it is not inherited as an overridable method','Private methods are not inherited for overriding.'),(2789,35,'Can an overriding method have more permissive access than the overridden method?','MEDIUM','Yes','An override may widen access but cannot reduce it.'),(2790,35,'Which access modifier is suitable when a member should be accessible to subclasses outside its package?','MEDIUM','protected','protected provides subclass access outside the declaring package.'),(2791,35,'Which statement about package-private members is correct?','MEDIUM','They are accessible to other classes in the same package','Package-private access is limited to the same package.'),(2792,35,'Why can a public class be inaccessible from another package?','MEDIUM','Its enclosing package or another required type may not be accessible, or it may not be on the classpath','Public visibility does not override package/module accessibility or classpath requirements.'),(2793,22,'Which keyword is used to execute a block when an if condition is false?','EASY','else','The else block executes when the associated if condition evaluates to false.');
